{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require venues to accept government evidence of disability or caring needs",
        "additional_details": "Many disabled people and carers already have government evidence (PIP, DLA, Carer's Allowance letters), yet many venues only accept a paid for third-party card or require repeatedly submitting private medical data to third-party systems. This petition asks the Government to require venues and event organisers to accept existing government-issued evidence of disability or caring responsibilities, rather than requiring a paid card or repeated submission of private medical data to third-party systems.",
        "background": "Require venues and event organisers to accept existing government evidence (PIP, DLA, Carer's Allowance letters) for disability or caring needs, instead of forcing people to purchase a third-party card or repeatedly share private medical data for reasonable adjustments.",
